swift"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Discussion","anchor":"discussion"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A is the weighted adjacency matrix: parallel edges add their weights, self-loops are"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"ignored, and a weight of 0 is no edge. The eigenvalues are sorted ascending with their"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"multiplicity, so a graph with c components has c zero eigenvalues and its axes come from"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"eigenvectors of 0 when c > 1 (which ones is fixed by the solver, not specified). Each axis’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"sign makes its first entry, in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"vertices"},{"type":"text","text":" order, whose magnitude is at least 10⁻⁴ of its"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"largest positive. Two vertices have y = 0, and one vertex is at the origin. The drawing is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"not rescaled ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"rescaled(scale:center:)"},{"type":"text","text":" maps it to a common frame). A directed graph is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"drawn through "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"undirectedView"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Dense: Householder tridiagonalization and the implicit QL iteration, O(n³) time and n²"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Double"},{"type":"text","text":"s, for graphs of up to a few thousand vertices."}]},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Koren, “Drawing graphs by eigenvectors: theory and practice”, Computers & Mathematics with"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Applications 49(11–12), 2005."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]},{"style":"note","type":"aside","name":"Precondition","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Every weight is finite and not negative; ","type":"text"},{"code":"maxIterations","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", when given, is at","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"least 1.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"style":"note","type":"aside","name":"Throws","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"NoConvergence"},{"text":" after ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"maxIterations"},{"text":" QL iterations in all (30 n when nil), with","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"that count and the off-diagonal entry being reduced, relative to the largest entry of its","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"block. The iteration converges cubically, about two iterations per eigenvalue.","type":"text"}]}]}],"kind":"content"}],"sections":[],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/graphdrawing\/graphprotocols\/graph\/spectrallayout(weight:maxiterations:)"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"abstract":[{"text":"A drawing whose axes are eigenvectors of the Laplacian: x is the eigenvector of the second","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"smallest eigenvalue of L = D − A (the Fiedler vector of a connected graph) and y that of","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the third, both of unit length, in ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"vertices"},{"text":" order.","type":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","references":{"doc://GraphDrawing/documentation/GraphDrawing":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphDrawing\/documentation\/GraphDrawing","title":"GraphDrawing","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/graphdrawing","role":"collection","abstract":[],"kind":"symbol"},"doc://GraphDrawing/documentation/GraphDrawing/GraphProtocols/Graph":{"abstract":[],"identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphDrawing\/documentation\/GraphDrawing\/GraphProtocols\/Graph","kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Graph"}],"url":"\/docum